==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*smakkijan|t=to taste}}, from *{{inh|de|gmw-pro|*smakku|t=a taste}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*smegʰ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*smeg-|t=to taste}}. Compare {{cog|en|smack}} and {{m|en|smatch}}, as well as Lithuanian {{m|lt|smagù||cheerful, enjoyable, pleasant}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|[ˈʃmɛkn̩]|[ˈʃmɛkŋ̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-schmecken.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɛkn̩|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|copulative|often with {{m|de|nach|tr=like}}}} to [[taste]] (good, bad, sweet, salty, etc.)
#: {{ux|de|Das Bier '''schmeckt''' sehr gut.|The beer tastes very good.}}
#: {{ux|de|Igitt, dieser Wein schmeckt nach Essig.|Yuck, this wine tastes like vinegar.}}
# to [[enjoy]] {{qual|the taste of something}}
#: {{ux|de|Hat es '''geschmeckt'''?|Did you enjoy it (the food)?}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|sometimes with dative}} to [[taste]] [[good]]
#: {{ux|de|Igitt! Das '''schmeckt''' nicht.|Yuck! That '''tastes''' bad.}}

